        "text": "=For context, today's date (DD-MM-YYYY) is: {{ $json.file.createTime.split('T')[0] }}\n\nThis is a receipt or expense-related image. Extract the following information as plain text for each distinct expense item: item name, total quantity, total amount paid (in RM if visible), payment method (if available), and date (if available, else default to current date). Be concise and specific.\n\nExtraction Rules:\n\ncategory: The broad category of the item. Must be exactly one of - Groceries, Dining out, Coffee & snacks, Fuel, Public transport, Ride-sharing & taxis, Parking & tolls, Home supplies, Home maintenance, Personal grooming, Personal health, Hobbies, Events & outings, Shopping, Pet food & treats, Pet care, Gifts, Other\n\nitem_name: Specific name of the product or service.\n\nquantity: The total count (integer or decimal).\n\namount_rm: Total amount paid in RM (number only).\n\npayment_method: Must be exactly one of - Touch n' Go, Cash, Credit/Debit Card, DuitNow, Bank Transfer, Grab, Shopee, Lazada, Unknown\n\ndate: ISO 8601 format (DD-MM-YYYY) if available, default to today's date if unspecified.\n\nOutput Format:\nReturn only a valid JSON object with an expenses key containing an array of objects. Do not include any introductory text or markdown explanations.\n\nIMPORTANT: If the message is NOT an expense (e.g. non-sensical words, greeting, or question like \"How are you today?\"), return: {\\\"error\\\": \\\"not_an_expense\\\"}",
        "imageUrls": "={{ $json.file.uri }}",
        "options": {}
      },
